## What Gets Updated Automatically

### 1. When a method is changed:
   - ✅ methods.json updated with new metadata
   - ✅ changelog.json gets new entry
   - ✅ flow-diagram.md regenerated
   - ✅ HTML shows updated status (new/enhanced/refactored)

### 2. When a new method is added:
   - ✅ Added to methods.json
   - ✅ Diagram includes new method
   - ✅ Changelog entry created
   - ✅ Marked as "new" in UI

### 3. When a method is deleted:
   - ✅ Marked as deleted in methods.json
   - ✅ Diagram updated to remove method
   - ✅ Changelog entry added

## Quick Update Command

For quick updates, use the auto-update script:
```bash
./docs/features/scripts/auto-update.sh <file1.ts> [file2.ts ...]
```

This automatically:
1. Detects which feature needs updating
2. Runs track-changes.js
3. Runs update-docs.js
4. Updates all related documentation

## Important Notes

- **ALWAYS run track-changes.js BEFORE update-docs.js**
- Diagrams are auto-generated from methods.json
- Changelog entries automatically include git info (commit, date, author)
- Methods metadata includes: file, line, type, parameters, returns, dependencies, execution paths, error handling, side effects
- **When user edits code that affects diagrams, YOU MUST automatically update the documentation**
